WEBVTT

01:29.980 --> 01:32.480
Yaki-
soba

01:29.980 --> 01:32.480
French
 Fries

01:30.270 --> 01:32.480
Episode 6: But I Get To Keep Charlotte

01:44.960 --> 01:46.000
Oh, look.

01:47.170 --> 01:48.100
Hey.

02:04.380 --> 02:07.630
What's wrong, little miss? Lost your mom?

02:14.640 --> 02:16.670
You kick too hard...

02:16.670 --> 02:18.110
Osanai-san.

02:20.020 --> 02:25.170
Sorry. I'm not used to wearing geta sandals.
 I couldn't fling it how I wanted to.

02:26.260 --> 02:27.560
Did it hurt?

02:28.240 --> 02:29.410
Severely.

02:31.550 --> 02:36.630
Your words hurt me a lot, though, Kobato-kun.

02:37.820 --> 02:40.300
So you'll forgive me, right?

02:41.680 --> 02:42.680
Of course.

02:43.560 --> 02:44.940
Great.

02:47.970 --> 02:49.810
Where did you get that?

02:50.210 --> 02:52.830
They were selling them
 at a woodcraft stall.

02:53.490 --> 02:54.730
Let's walk together.

02:59.670 --> 03:03.240
I take it there's someone up ahead 
you don't want to meet.

03:03.240 --> 03:04.050
Yeah.

03:04.050 --> 03:05.720
A classmate or someone?

03:05.720 --> 03:07.030
From a while back.

03:07.440 --> 03:09.170
Why not go back, then?

03:10.320 --> 03:13.210
I left my bike over there.

03:13.660 --> 03:14.600
Huh.

03:15.090 --> 03:16.610
Dressed like that?

03:19.130 --> 03:21.520
So, Osanai-san, how's exam study going?

03:22.640 --> 03:28.840
This is a key time in our schooling. We mustn't
 stay out late just because there's a festival.

03:29.990 --> 03:32.860
Would an ordinary person 
stick to that and miss out?

03:35.810 --> 03:37.820
That doesn't seem quite right.

03:37.820 --> 03:40.400
Rules are made to be broken.

03:40.400 --> 03:42.610
That's what you'd say before heading out.

03:43.230 --> 03:47.370
But you'd hide if you saw a teacher.

03:47.370 --> 03:54.120
<b>Chocolate banana</b>

03:47.650 --> 03:52.740
Yup. I think that's apt behavior for the 
"ordinary person" we aspire to become.

03:52.740 --> 03:53.430
Yeah.

03:55.390 --> 03:57.780
I forgot to get the cotton candy.

04:02.840 --> 04:05.640
Look at the time. We should head home.

04:06.440 --> 04:08.390
By the way, Kobato-kun...

04:08.390 --> 04:10.630
Do you have any plans for the summer?

04:11.040 --> 04:12.550
Nothing in particular.

04:12.550 --> 04:13.630
What about you?

04:14.040 --> 04:18.140
I have a feeling something 
fantastic is going to happen.

04:42.410 --> 04:46.140
Kobato-kun, do you know what this is?

04:51.220 --> 04:55.090
It's a map of several snack shops in town.

04:57.380 --> 04:59.960
That's right, but that's not it.

04:59.960 --> 05:01.090
What do you mean?

05:01.090 --> 05:02.060
This here...

05:03.250 --> 05:07.080
is going to determine 
my destiny this summer.

05:07.970 --> 05:08.950
Your destiny?

05:09.630 --> 05:13.300
Osanai Sweets Selection: Summer.

05:27.060 --> 05:30.500
Listen, I'm not that into sweet stuff.

05:35.690 --> 05:38.350
You won't accept it?

05:52.120 --> 05:58.370
<b>Kobato Japanese Confectionery</b>

05:52.520 --> 05:54.580
Okay, I'll take it.

05:54.580 --> 05:55.510
Good.

05:55.900 --> 05:58.380
Then, let's go to the shops tomorrow.

05:58.380 --> 06:00.510
With me, you mean?

06:00.510 --> 06:01.170
Yeah.

06:01.590 --> 06:02.800
What's going on?

06:02.800 --> 06:04.520
Is there a reason for this?

06:04.820 --> 06:11.510
It would really help to have someone like 
you to complete my plans for the summer.

06:15.050 --> 06:16.590
Don't you want to go?

06:17.060 --> 06:18.900
I don't mind, but...

06:19.620 --> 06:21.520
Okay. Great.

06:21.940 --> 06:23.860
Well, see you at one tomorrow.

06:38.530 --> 06:41.750
<i>"I'm sorry. Something came up, 
and I can't leave the house."</i>

06:38.540 --> 06:51.050
I'm sorry. Something came up, and I can't leave the house

06:41.540 --> 06:51.050
Please go to Shop Number 10, buy two mango puddings,

06:41.750 --> 06:44.850
<i>"Please go to Shop Number 10,
 buy two mango puddings,</i>

06:44.630 --> 06:51.050
and four grapefruit Charlotte cakes,

06:44.850 --> 06:50.040
<i>and four grapefruit Charlotte cakes,
 then bring them to my place."</i>

06:48.010 --> 06:51.050
then bring them to my place

06:50.040 --> 06:51.040
<i>"Sorry."</i>

06:50.180 --> 06:51.050
Sorry

07:30.720 --> 07:34.220
Charlotte

07:31.300 --> 07:32.830
One short.

07:32.830 --> 07:34.220
Welcome.

07:35.050 --> 07:39.630
Hi. Will the cakes here 
get refilled if I wait long enough?

07:39.630 --> 07:41.810
This is all we have.

07:43.220 --> 07:44.650
I see.

07:45.080 --> 07:50.600
In that case, two mango puddings 
and three Charlottes, please.

07:53.610 --> 07:55.620
I bought the cakes

07:55.620 --> 07:57.620
Thanks. I can't wait

08:02.870 --> 08:05.500
Sorry to send you shopping.

08:05.500 --> 08:06.710
It must have been hot.

08:07.070 --> 08:10.730
I don't mind shopping, 
but it was ridiculously hot.

08:37.540 --> 08:39.510
Well, shall we eat?

08:39.510 --> 08:40.290
Yeah.

08:49.200 --> 08:51.480
Hello? Well?

08:52.070 --> 08:52.930
Yeah.

08:53.610 --> 08:55.730
Yeah. Yeah.

08:55.730 --> 08:58.030
Oh, sorry, one second.

09:00.320 --> 09:02.060
Just give me a minute.

09:53.610 --> 09:55.400
Maybe I should get started.

11:14.860 --> 11:17.860
There are two more Charlottes

11:32.620 --> 11:35.130
Here's what I'll have her believe:

11:36.750 --> 11:41.010
There were only ever two Charlottes

11:41.710 --> 11:43.080
The TV remote.

11:43.740 --> 11:45.260
The AC remote.

11:45.820 --> 11:48.000
An unopened box of tissues.

11:49.040 --> 11:52.040
Two mango puddings. Untouched.

11:52.580 --> 11:56.200
Two Charlottes. Untouched. Exquisite.

11:57.160 --> 11:59.040
Two cake boxes.

11:59.510 --> 12:00.720
Paper napkins.

12:00.720 --> 12:02.340
Cake holders.

12:02.340 --> 12:03.400
Cooler packs.

12:03.790 --> 12:07.690
A receipt for two mango puddings 
and three Charlottes.

12:12.670 --> 12:14.670
A thick, gold paper saucer.

12:15.120 --> 12:16.140
A spoon.

12:16.560 --> 12:19.400
Plastic film with Bavarian cream on it.

12:19.400 --> 12:21.220
No evidence on the small plate.

12:22.080 --> 12:25.000
A spoon for Osanai-san to use.

12:25.570 --> 12:27.280
Two coffee cups.

12:27.670 --> 12:29.010
A cup of barley tea.

12:39.940 --> 12:42.320
Take 1

12:39.940 --> 12:42.320
Reduce the three 
cake holders to two

13:01.510 --> 13:03.340
What are you up to, Kobato-kun?

13:10.350 --> 13:12.600
Take 2

13:10.350 --> 13:12.600
Pretend there were never 
any cake holders to begin with

13:23.360 --> 13:25.610
Four more

13:23.360 --> 13:25.610
It takes 
even longer

13:35.810 --> 13:37.760
How do I, in the shortest time,

13:37.760 --> 13:40.850
make it impossible to deduce from the 
cake holders how many cakes there were?

13:54.730 --> 13:56.310
One, two.

13:56.830 --> 13:58.470
One, two.

13:58.470 --> 13:59.270
Okay.

14:20.810 --> 14:23.050
The Charlotte is mine.

14:24.560 --> 14:28.540
I've left no evidence.

14:32.550 --> 14:33.930
Shoot

14:35.680 --> 14:38.190
It's so hot.
Why would I have coffee 
instead of barley tea?

14:45.750 --> 14:47.070
Screw it.

14:53.420 --> 14:55.290
Yup. Can't tell.

14:58.170 --> 14:59.410
Mango pudding.

14:59.730 --> 15:02.500
Thanks. I was looking forward to this.

15:02.500 --> 15:04.030
You're welcome.

15:04.290 --> 15:06.300
Huh? The Charlottes...

15:06.300 --> 15:07.340
Oh, yeah.

15:07.610 --> 15:10.180
It seems they're pretty popular.

15:10.180 --> 15:12.180
They only had two left.

15:13.360 --> 15:16.470
Oh. They were sold out?

15:19.580 --> 15:21.910
Well, let's eat.

15:29.060 --> 15:31.860
Oh, I'm keeping my favorite for later.

15:32.520 --> 15:33.610
I see.

15:33.610 --> 15:37.230
Sorry my call took so long. 
What did you do while you were waiting?

15:38.950 --> 15:42.110
Oh, yeah, I was just chilling.

15:43.620 --> 15:45.230
This room, though...

15:46.920 --> 15:50.880
Wasn't it hot in here? It's set to 27 degrees.

15:56.310 --> 16:00.020
I can't bring myself to mess with someone 
else's appliances without permission.

16:00.020 --> 16:02.130
You don't need to worry about that.

16:02.630 --> 16:04.320
But I guess that makes sense.

16:04.810 --> 16:06.860
Sorry I didn't notice.

16:11.640 --> 16:13.730
I knew it would be good.

16:14.110 --> 16:18.880
I don't know if I should say this, 
but this has to be my favorite so far.

16:20.970 --> 16:24.270
I can recommend more 
if you like this kind of thing.

16:25.700 --> 16:27.270
Tell me about them sometime.

16:27.270 --> 16:28.000
Sure.

16:49.150 --> 16:51.150
There were two napkins...

16:52.900 --> 16:54.660
How many over here?

16:55.910 --> 16:58.160
If there were three...

16:58.330 --> 16:59.330
Kobato-kun?

17:00.910 --> 17:03.400
I wonder why they're called Charlottes.

17:04.040 --> 17:07.730
Well, you see, a Charlotte is a kind of hat.

17:07.730 --> 17:12.420
These are single serving-sized, 
but the whole cake is shaped like a hat, too.

17:12.420 --> 17:15.730
Huh. Have you had a whole one before?

17:16.700 --> 17:18.540
Only once.

17:37.280 --> 17:38.600
Oh, sorry.

17:39.780 --> 17:40.980
Just a second.

17:46.130 --> 17:47.690
Sorry.

17:48.350 --> 17:50.250
The garbage bin's over there.

18:14.850 --> 18:16.490
By the way, Kobato-kun...

18:17.740 --> 18:22.140
They hide sauce inside these cakes.

18:22.140 --> 18:23.580
What do you think it is?

18:24.870 --> 18:26.530
There's sauce inside?

18:26.920 --> 18:28.920
I haven't gotten that far yet.

18:29.390 --> 18:30.560
Really?

18:31.260 --> 18:32.350
But...

18:34.120 --> 18:36.390
You've had it before, haven't you?

18:49.230 --> 18:51.710
Yeah. I have.

18:51.710 --> 18:53.990
It was like marmalade.

18:55.420 --> 18:56.600
It was good.

18:57.060 --> 19:00.790
You really liked Jeff Beck's
 Charlottes, huh?

19:01.330 --> 19:02.820
It was the best.

19:03.500 --> 19:06.580
I'm glad you liked them so much.

19:07.060 --> 19:08.660
I love them, too.

19:09.360 --> 19:12.540
So why did you think to do this?

19:12.540 --> 19:15.060
Again, because it was so good.

19:15.060 --> 19:16.990
Yup, you mentioned that.

19:16.990 --> 19:20.000
So why did you think to do this?

19:25.620 --> 19:28.180
Because it was just the two of us.

19:28.630 --> 19:29.980
In other words,

19:29.980 --> 19:35.180
because you thought you'd be free 
to challenge me if it's just me and you?

19:37.000 --> 19:40.440
Did you think it'd be fun 
if you could deceive me?

19:46.760 --> 19:50.230
There were three Charlottes, weren't there?

19:50.230 --> 19:52.570
They only had three left.

19:55.760 --> 19:58.270
You're coming with me all summer.

19:58.270 --> 20:02.030
We're going to all those shops from
 yesterday, up to my number one.

20:07.540 --> 20:09.830
I still don't get it.

20:09.830 --> 20:11.760
Where did I slip up?

20:12.260 --> 20:16.350
It couldn't have been easy for you 
to figure out there were three cakes.

20:17.680 --> 20:21.560
Because, Kobato-kun, you wiped 
away your sweat with a tissue.

20:22.580 --> 20:27.990
You were wiping away your sweat with 
a handkerchief when you first came in.

20:27.990 --> 20:32.870
But after spilling your coffee,
 you used a tissue.

20:33.620 --> 20:40.000
That's how I knew the handkerchief must
 have become unusable while I was away.

20:40.440 --> 20:44.000
The fact that you couldn't 
use your handkerchief

20:44.000 --> 20:48.920
means you'd used it to wipe off 
something else and couldn't pull it out.

20:49.560 --> 20:52.630
What could have dirtied it so much
 you couldn't take it out?

20:53.150 --> 20:56.900
There was only the Bavarian cream 
in the room that could have done that.

21:01.460 --> 21:06.750
You probably wouldn't have figured it out if 
I hadn't used my handkerchief when I came in.

21:09.130 --> 21:10.580
I think you're right.

21:10.580 --> 21:17.370
But if I hadn't noticed at all, 
you would surely have given me a hint.

21:17.740 --> 21:20.020
You wouldn't enjoy a flawless victory.

21:20.560 --> 21:22.130
I know you well enough.

21:24.350 --> 21:26.110
I wouldn't do that.
